// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`The properties panel > has six tabs, and every option on every tab says what it does 1`] = `
"a full-time agent › Overview › Ask a question — A side chat: it answers from what it knows, and its work goes on.
a full-time agent › Overview › Stop VP — Stops its task now, after a question. Its conversation stays.
a full-time agent › Overview › Objective for VP — Say what it should get done. It can hand parts of it to its team. Enter sends. Shift and Enter start a new line.
a full-time agent › Overview › Give objective — Its agent starts on it now, in its first conversation.
a full-time agent › Overview › Open its page — Its work, history, and permissions on a page of its own.
a full-time agent › Job › Add your own specialty — Write a specialty of your own for the VP role.
a full-time agent › Job › This agent learns — Whether it writes down lessons from its work and gets its role's kept lessons.
a full-time agent › Job › VP agents learn — On or off for every VP agent without a setting of its own.
a full-time agent › Job › Learn on its own — On: this role's lessons are kept without asking you. Only lessons from tasks that used no tools are kept without you; the rest wait for your review.
a full-time agent › AI model › See every rule — Settings → AI models: the rules for the organization, departments, roles, and agents.
a full-time agent › AI model › AI tool — Automatic: the rules pick the AI tool and model, and say why. Or fix one for this agent.
a full-time agent › AI model › Model — The model this AI tool runs for this agent.
a full-time agent › AI model › Save AI tool and model — Keeps the AI tool and model chosen above for this agent.
a full-time agent › AI model › Effort — How hard the model thinks before it answers. Changing it never hires a new agent.
a full-time agent › AI model › Give it its own rule — Models, efforts, and AI companies for this agent alone; its rule comes before all others.
a full-time agent › Work › Change permissions — Settings → Permissions: what each role may do, and each project's limit.
a full-time agent › Team › Move to report to — Its whole team moves with it.
a full-time agent › Team › Move — Makes it report to the one chosen above.
a full-time agent › Manage › Title — Unique within its team; teammates hand work to each other by title.
a full-time agent › Manage › Rename — Keeps the new title. Its agent and conversation stay.
a full-time agent › Manage › Hire into team — Add a position to its team: a new agent, or one from your Workforce.
a full-time agent › Manage › Let agent go — Its agent retires and its conversation ends; the position stays, vacant.
a full-time agent › Manage › Archive — Takes it off the chart; you can bring it back, save it to your Workforce, or delete it for good.
an on-call agent › Overview › Stop Senior Developer — Stops its workers' tasks now, after a question.
an on-call agent › Overview › Open its page — Its work, history, and permissions on a page of its own.
an on-call agent › Job › Specialty — Adds lines for one area of work to its instructions. Changing it never hires a new agent.
an on-call agent › Job › Add your own specialty — Write a specialty of your own for the Senior Developer role.
an on-call agent › Job › This agent learns — Whether it writes down lessons from its work and gets its role's kept lessons.
an on-call agent › Job › Senior Developer agents learn — On or off for every Senior Developer agent without a setting of its own.
an on-call agent › Job › Remove — Remove takes a lesson out of the instructions of Senior Developer's later workers.
an on-call agent › Job › Learn on its own — On: this role's lessons are kept without asking you. Only lessons from tasks that used no tools are kept without you; the rest wait for your review.
an on-call agent › AI model › See every rule — Settings → AI models: the rules for the organization, departments, roles, and agents.
an on-call agent › AI model › AI tool — Automatic: the rules pick the AI tool and model, and say why. Or fix one for this agent.
an on-call agent › AI model › Save AI tool and model — Keeps the AI tool and model chosen above for this agent.
an on-call agent › AI model › Effort — How hard the model thinks before it answers. Changing it never hires a new agent.
an on-call agent › AI model › Give it its own rule — Models, efforts, and AI companies for this agent alone; its rule comes before all others.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › See every rule — Settings → AI models: the rules for the organization, departments, roles, and agents.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › AI tool — Automatic: the rules pick the AI tool and model, and say why. Or fix one for this agent.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › Save AI tool and model — Keeps the AI tool and model chosen above for this agent.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › Effort — How hard the model thinks before it answers. Changing it never hires a new agent.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › Effort for Opus (Claude Code) — The first model that is ready gets the work; the backups are tried in order. Each model's effort is how hard it thinks. Remove takes a model off this list.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › Move Opus (Claude Code) up — The first model that is ready gets the work; the backups are tried in order. Each model's effort is how hard it thinks. Remove takes a model off this list.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › Move Opus (Claude Code) down — The first model that is ready gets the work; the backups are tried in order. Each model's effort is how hard it thinks. Remove takes a model off this list.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › Take Opus (Claude Code) off the list — The first model that is ready gets the work; the backups are tried in order. Each model's effort is how hard it thinks. Remove takes a model off this list.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › Add a model to the list — Adds it at the end. Every AI tool's models are here, your subscriptions first; one not in Your models yet is added there too.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › Effort for any other model — How hard a model thinks when this rule does not name it above. A model that does not take this level keeps its own.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › Save rule — Save keeps this rule; Remove rule lets the rules around it decide. A new effort reaches open conversations with their next task, and never hires a new agent.
an on-call agent › AI model (its own rule) › Cancel — Save keeps this rule; Remove rule lets the rules around it decide. A new effort reaches open conversations with their next task, and never hires a new agent.
an on-call agent › Work › Change permissions — Settings → Permissions: what each role may do, and each project's limit.
an on-call agent › Team › Move to report to — It joins the chosen lead's team.
an on-call agent › Team › Move — Makes it report to the one chosen above.
an on-call agent › Team › Lend to the team of — Its lead can hand it work while it helps.
an on-call agent › Team › For how long — One objective, or until you press Send home.
an on-call agent › Team › Lend — It helps that team, under that team's project's limits, and comes home when you choose (or when that objective is done).
an on-call agent › Team › Assign as — What it checks for the team: its work, its testing, or its safety.
an on-call agent › Team › Of the team led by — The lead whose team hands it work to check.
an on-call agent › Team › Assign — It stays where it is and joins that team's list of who checks the work.
an on-call agent › Manage › Title — Unique within its team; teammates hand work to each other by title.
an on-call agent › Manage › Rename — Keeps the new title. Its agent and conversation stay.
an on-call agent › Manage › Archive — Takes it off the chart; you can bring it back, save it to your Workforce, or delete it for good.
a manager › Overview › Ask a question — A side chat: it answers from what it knows, and its work goes on.
a manager › Overview › Objective for Engineering Manager — Say what it should get done. It can hand parts of it to its team. Enter sends. Shift and Enter start a new line.
